course: dictionary
lesson: 11372
title: Abnormal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abnormal means not normal, not usual, or different from what you expect. Often it is a sign that something may be wrong. Look at the start of the word: "ab" means away from, so abnormal is away from the usual pattern.
explain: «The doctor said the blood test showed an abnormal result, so she ran the test again.» The result did not fit the healthy pattern, so the doctor checked it a second time. The word abnormal tells you the result was different and worth looking at.
explain: In science and maths, abnormal can mean outside the usual range. «The temperature was abnormally high for January.» Abnormally is the adverb form, and it tells you how the temperature was high: in an unusual way. To check your meaning, swap in "unusual" or "strange" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Abnormal means not normal, not usual, or different from what is expected.
fact: «Abnormal» often suggests that something is strange or worrying.
fact: «Abnormally» is the adverb form: «The river rose abnormally fast after the storm.»
fact: In science and health, «abnormal» means outside the healthy or typical range, like an abnormal heartbeat.
fact: In data, a value far away from the rest is sometimes called an outlier, and it can be described as abnormal.
exercise: «The sky was abnormally dark at noon, so the streetlights came on.» What does abnormal suggest here? | Very cheerful and bright | Quiet and calm | Exactly the same as every day | *Not usual, different from what is expected
exercise: «Ella's dog ate a whole cake and was unwell, which was abnormal for him.» Find and copy the word that means not usual. | unwell | cake | *abnormal | dog
exercise: The doctor said the heartbeat was abnormal, so she checked it again. Why would she do that? | Because abnormal means very happy | Because the heartbeat is always fine | Because abnormal means the same as before | *Because it is outside the healthy pattern, which could be a warning
test: «His behaviour was abnormal: he stayed silent all day, which was not like him.» What does abnormal mean here? | Normal for him | Very tidy | *Different from usual | Loud and cheerful
test: Which word is the adverb form of abnormal? | abnormal | normal | normally | *abnormally
exam: Which sentence uses abnormal correctly? | I felt abnormal because I was eating my lunch in the park. | *The test result was abnormal, so the doctor ran it again. | The abnormal sun shone on the normal day, so it was boring. | Abnormal means the same as breakfast.
